menu "Apple"

config SND_SOC_APPLE_MCA
	tristate "Apple Silicon MCA driver"
	depends on ARCH_APPLE || COMPILE_TEST
	select SND_DMAENGINE_PCM
	help
	  This option enables an ASoC platform driver for MCA peripherals found
	  on Apple Silicon SoCs.

config SND_SOC_APPLE_S8000_MCA
	tristate "Apple S8000/T8010 MCA driver"
	depends on ARCH_APPLE || COMPILE_TEST
	depends on COMMON_CLK
	select MFD_SYSCON
	select SND_SOC_GENERIC_DMAENGINE_PCM
	help
	  This option enables an ASoC CPU DAI driver for the "mca-version 4"
	  I2S serializer of the Apple A9 (S8000/S8003), and the version 5
	  serializer of the A10 (T8010). The driver also
	  exports the MCA's MCLK output as a clock for the codec and routes
	  the MCA to its pad in the shared i2s-switch. Samples are moved by
	  SmartIO DMA, so APPLE_SIO_DMA is needed for audio.

	  Say Y or M here if you have an Apple A9 device such as the iPad 5 or iPad 6.

config SND_SOC_APPLE_T8010_PDM
	tristate "Apple T8010 PDM capture (experimental)"
	depends on ARCH_APPLE || COMPILE_TEST
	depends on OF && DMA_ENGINE && EXPERT
	depends on APPLE_AOP_AUDIO && APPLE_SIO_DMA
	help
	  Build the experimental T8010 microphone consumer for development.
	  This is not microphone enablement: no board node or sound card is
	  supplied. A firmware-owned PDM clock and live calibration are needed.
	  Requires ownership-preserving SmartIO drain and exclusive AOP clock
	  ownership. Faulted teardown may wait until a device reset.
	  Do not enable a board node until these contracts are verified.
	  If unsure, say N.

config SND_SOC_APPLE_T8010_PDM_KUNIT_TEST
	tristate "T8010 PDM calibration arithmetic tests" if !KUNIT_ALL_TESTS
	depends on KUNIT
	default KUNIT_ALL_TESTS
	help
	  Test calibration bounds, register packing and capture discard sizing
	  using synthetic inputs. The tests do not access hardware or enable
	  the microphone driver. No firmware or factory calibration is used.
	  These tests do not establish safe DMA lifetime or audio quality.

endmenu
